Many Moria players forsook Moria in favour of Angband.  Angband has in
its turn begotten a plethora of variants, especially subsequent to Ben
Harrison's sterling work in cleaning up the source code during the 2.7
and 2.8 releases.

Angband feels very different indeed to Nethack, and Dungeon Crawl has
features in common with both, as well as distinctive features of its
own; I prefer Crawl's magic system over any other roguelike magic system
I've encountered, but wish the game was slightly less liable to
"Surprise! You're dead!" moments :)

